<p>Venezuela’s new amnesty law is starting to lead to prisoner releases. A Venezuelan nonprofit says it has verified 16 releases of people it considers political prisoners. The government is promoting the law as a path to freedom, and it has already prompted a wave of applications: more than 1,500 people have requested amnesty, according to reporting on the process. But the rollout is also fueling fresh tension behind bars. More than 200 political prisoners launched a hunger strike after learning they were excluded from the law’s benefits, demanding to be included and released. Opposition figures have criticized the legislation, saying its carve-outs could still let authorities pursue some offenses that have been used against Maduro’s opponents. Taken together, the early releases, the surge of applications, and the hunger strike highlight both the immediate human stakes and the disputed politics over how far the amnesty reaches.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/i6uT4HCc-Aepfi1WPlq1qzju4tZ2UpcHNTFuNQkoWpw0JZbTtvVR2aTL2pUjA7E8pTi-NP5F61i2eAcyuVKQ_rcAnm-_aVf2-4_VX3jBPzNqTP3mDGDGWaR3TM99xnQYd_7-XVS6hfiNeRpSt2FeonCNS5USjDGUBBzU8oTKwSs2sYlKmA' alt='People take part in a vigil to demand the freedom of political prisoners outside the El Helicoide building, headquarters of the Bolivarian National Intelligence Service (SEBIN), Caracas, Venezuela, February 21, 2026.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Verification gap: Rights monitors are confirming releases one by one, and they say the independently verified tally still lags official claims as the process begins to move.</li><li>Exclusion trigger: Hunger strikers say they took action after being told they were not covered by the new amnesty provisions, and they want to be included and released.</li><li>Applications surge: More than 1,500 people have filed amnesty requests, showing how many detainees and families are trying to use the new legal pathway.</li></ul><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>Venezuelan nonprofit/rights monitors: A nonprofit tracking detentions says it is verifying releases one by one, and argues the confirmed count remains far below what authorities say the amnesty has delivered. (<a href='https://abcnews.com/International/wireStory/venezuelan-nonprofit-16-verified-prisoners-released-venezuelas-amnesty-130393402'>ABC News</a>)</li><li>Hunger-striking prisoners: Detainees taking part in the protest say the amnesty leaves many of them out, and they are demanding to be covered and released. (<a href='https://www.straitstimes.com/world/more-than-200-political-prisoners-in-venezuela-launch-hunger-strike'>The Straits Times</a>)</li><li>Opposition figures: Opposition leaders criticize the amnesty legislation, saying its carve-outs could still allow prosecutions under charges used in past cases against opponents. (<a href='https://www.thehindu.com/news/international/more-than-1500-request-amnesty-under-new-venezuela-law/article70663693.ece'>The Hindu</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://abcnews.com/International/wireStory/venezuelan-nonprofit-16-verified-prisoners-released-venezuelas-amnesty-130393402'>Venezuelan nonprofit says 16 verified prisoners released under Venezuela’s amnesty</a> - abcnews.com</li><li><a href='https://www.thehindu.com/news/international/more-than-1500-request-amnesty-under-new-venezuela-law/article70663693.ece'>More than 1,500 request amnesty under new Venezuela law</a> - thehindu.com</li><li><a href='https://www.firstpost.com/world/more-than-200-venezuelan-political-prisoners-launch-hunger-strike-over-limits-of-new-amnesty-law-ws-e-13982658.html'>More than 200 Venezuelan political prisoners launch hunger strike over limits of new amnesty law</a> - firstpost.com</li><li><a href='https://www.straitstimes.com/world/more-than-200-political-prisoners-in-venezuela-launch-hunger-strike'>More than 200 political prisoners in Venezuela launch hunger strike</a> - straitstimes.com</li><li><a href='https://www.lemonde.fr/en/international/article/2026/02/23/more-than-200-political-prisoners-in-venezuela-launch-hunger-strike_6750766_4.html'>Over 200 political prisoners in Venezuela launch hunger strike</a> - lemonde.fr</li></ul>